    "matches_claimed_nav_left": false,
    "honesty": "applied_vx is the clamped command, not odometry. Forward clamp is 0.056 m/s, lowered from 0.080 because 0.080 yaws off and tips near 1.2 m (support margin about \u22120.09 m). CPG amplitude is |applied_vx| / 0.080, so full forward stick is amplitude 0.70 and reverse -0.032 m/s stays amplitude 0.40 with stance damper 100 N/(m/s). Yaw cap is \u00b10.25 rad/s. Forward yaw is swing-phase only: stance hip yaw is 0, and the airborne foot toes 0.10 rad left or 0.12 rad right at full stick (+joint toes right). Outside-step scale stays 0.20 on a left command (0.24 after 12 s) and 0.10 on a right command. Forward swing adds 0.38 rad of knee flexion at mid-swing and scales contralateral shoulder pitch by 3.4. Lateral COM shift is 0.16 rad. Reverse does not take the knee lift or the arm scale. Measured motion \u0394x=+0.742 m, mean body vx=+0.046 m/s (not the command). Straight-forward net yaw drift=+4.09 deg; yaw during that window -2.2 to +5.3 deg. Heading at the end of the clip is +52.09 deg from the start. Turn-window \u0394yaw=+58.68 deg (mean yaw rate +0.082 rad/s, cap \u00b10.25). tip=False; CoP in box=True (outside 0.0000 m); peak leg torque=2.10 Nm (limit 2.1). Stance-slip damper is 25 N/(m/s) while walking forward, down from the CSF50 crawl's 115. After stop it is 100 N/(m/s) for 1.20 s (pose blend 0.70 s), then off. A reverse stop finishes at most one step first if that phase would pitch. Foot box, friction, kp, and \u00b12.1 Nm are unchanged. Nav: approach \u0394x=+0.742 m (mean body vx +0.046 m/s), turn \u0394yaw=+58.7 deg (mean yaw rate +0.082 rad/s, mean body vx +0.036 m/s), resume along heading +0.311 m (mean body vx +0.049 m/s)."
  },
